-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ACTION REQUIRED BEFORE DISTRIBUTING
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The full text of the GNU Affero General Public License version 3 must be
appended below this line. It could not be fetched automatically because
gnu.org is not reachable from the environment this file was written in.

    curl -o AGPL-3.0.txt https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.txt
    cat AGPL-3.0.txt >> LICENSE

The AGPL applies to this directory's `plugin/` subtree, which links JUCE.
JUCE 8 is dual-licensed AGPLv3-or-commercial, and BD-VHS sets
JUCE_DISPLAY_SPLASH_SCREEN=0, which is only permitted under the AGPL or a paid
JUCE licence. Choosing the AGPL is what makes that setting lawful here.

The DSP core in `core/` has no JUCE dependency and is MIT licensed instead --
see core/LICENSE. That split is deliberate: the core stays reusable in projects
that cannot take on the AGPL.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
TRADEMARK NOTICE
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

BD-VHS is an original effect inspired by the sound of tape and video-cassette
degradation. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or derived from any pedal
manufacturer's product, and contains no third-party trademarks. The machine
profiles are designed by ear from the characteristic response of each class of
recording machine, not measured from any specific product.
